From: DualMesh overlay
Subject: [PATCH] companion_radio: mount SPIFFS from the "mc_data" partition label

../partitions_dualmesh.csv gives Meshtastic's data partition the literal
label "spiffs" (required — stock Meshtastic code mounts by that exact
label with no override available at this call site) and gives MeshCore's
equivalent data partition the distinct label "mc_data" (ESP-IDF partition
tables require unique names, so both sides can't be called "spiffs").
Arduino-ESP32's SPIFFS.begin() takes the partition label as an optional
4th argument (default "spiffs") — this patch just supplies ours instead
of accepting that default, so this exact same global `SPIFFS` object (and
everything downstream of it, e.g. `DataStore store(SPIFFS, rtc_clock);`
declared earlier in this file) ends up backed by the correct partition.

Verified against ripplebiz/MeshCore @ main (HEAD 0679dbe as of 2026-08-30),
examples/companion_radio/main.cpp, lines 173-175.
---
--- a/examples/companion_radio/main.cpp
+++ b/examples/companion_radio/main.cpp
@@ -172,6 +172,7 @@
   );
 #elif defined(ESP32)
-  SPIFFS.begin(true);
+  SPIFFS.begin(true, "/spiffs", 10, "mc_data"); // DualMesh: use the "mc_data" partition,
+                                                  // not "spiffs" (that one's Meshtastic's)
   store.begin();
   the_mesh.begin(
     #ifdef DISPLAY_CLASS
